   "titulo": "The second family",
   "texto": [
    "The other type of adjectives behaves like a name. They are called adjectives in **-na** because they carry **な** when they go in front of a name: **しずか な まち** (quiet city), **ゆうめい な こうえん** (famous park).",
    "At the end of the sentence they do not carry: **この まち は しずか です** (this city is quiet).",
    "They refuse the same name as the names: **しずか じゃ ありません** (not quiet)."
   ]
